  "schema": "bd-mutate-spec/1",
  "_comment": "Row 686, generation be. Cloak browser reach is an OPTIONAL capability (operator ruling 2026-09-04): an absent requirements-cloak.txt and a failed launch/render probe are NAMED NON-FATAL degradations that set the cloak state and let the deploy of everything else finish. M10 and M11 re-introduce the two die calls the ruling removed and must be caught by the deploy-continues assertions. M13-M21 freeze each of the three cloak states at each of the three reporting surfaces -- the step [12] health report, the step [13] summary disposition and the deployed-capability record -- because a capability that never stops a deploy is legible only through what it reports. Every anchor matches structural text (a shell variable reference or a branch keyword) with the surrounding literal carried in fixed-width lookaround.",
  "subject": "row 686 - an absent or unreachable cloak browser degrades the deploy by name at three reporting surfaces instead of stopping it",
  "band": [
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_deploy_installs_and_renders_with_the_cloak_browser",
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_a_wrong_rendered_marker_is_unknown_reach_not_a_deploy_stop",
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_deploy_names_failed_browser_install_as_degradation_when_reach_works",
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_a_cloak_browser_that_cannot_launch_is_unknown_and_deploy_continues",
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_an_absent_cloak_manifest_is_absent_and_deploy_continues",
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_cloak_manifest_non_ok_dispositions_are_named[unknown]",
    "tests/test_deploy_script.py::test_cloak_manifest_non_ok_dispositions_are_named[absent]",
